<div style="text-align: center">

# <span style="color: #e6a050">Streamlined Logistics</span>

*<span style="color: #e6a050">Now, you can opt out of the Inventory Management™ minigame.</span>*

<div style="text-align: center">

*The source code for all my Enshrouded mods is available on [GitHub](https://github.com/Fuzen777/Enshrouded-Mods) (MIT)*

</div>

</div>

Tired of stopping every five minutes because your inventory is, *yet again*, full ? Streamlined Logistics is intended as an all-in-one storage mod for **Kiln** that solves this exact issue through automation.

Press **F2** and every chest you linked shows up as one searchable list next to your hotbars and backpack. Take what you need, drag it where you want it, store your loot, or let Quick Deposit and Re-Sort put everything into the right chests for you. Need a specific item ? Just open the menu : your favorited ones wait for you at the top, and everything else is searchable and neatly organized in tabs and categories.

If you fully set it up, you'll never have to worry about your inventory again :

- Enable Auto Quick Deposit, Salvage and Rename.
- Have a few unnamed Magic Chests around
- Whenever your inventory is full, its contents will be automatically deposited in your chests, and as you loot, items you don’t want get salvaged. Works with mods like [Kiln Auto Loot](https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/355).
- Coming from a chaotic, unorganized save ? Just click Re-Sort, and all your chests will be (almost) perfectly sorted without requiring you to do anything.

… This way, you’ll stop fighting your inventory so you can actually play the game. Most features are fully configurable if you’d rather have more inventory management in your game. I’m not judging. ||(I am.)||

---

## Features

### Control Center

The F2 menu offers :

- **Linked Chests** on the left, your **Hotbars** and **Inventory** on the right, with every item totalled across all linked chests.
- **Grid or list view**. Gear is listed per level and rarity.
- **Navigation sidebar** next to the stored items: every group and category with its count. Click one to jump straight to it. The sidebar folds away to a thin strip when you don't need it.
- **Resizable**: the window remembers its size and still opens centered. Drag the bar between the two sides to give your chests or your backpack more room.
- **Search**: every word you type must be in the item's name, in any order. By default a search looks through every category, whatever tab is open (**Search Every Tab**, can be turned off).
- **Category tree** built from the game's own data and curated for the occasional straggler : Gear, Consumables, Placeables, Building, Other and Materials, each with sub-categories (Weapons, Shields, Armor, Cosmetics, Rings, Tools, Meals, Raw Food, Potions, Ammo, Spells, Stations, Functional, Furniture, Seedlings and more).
- **Category tabs** (All, Favorites, then each group), headers that fold and stay folded, and like items kept together (all tiers of one item side by side, all tools next to each other).
- **Ungroup** to see the content chest by chest instead of one merged list.
- **Item details on hover** : for any item you have looked at in the game's own screens this session, the tooltip shows the game's full item detail (damage, perks, gems, description). Other items show the rows of the game's own tooltip (food effects and duration, spell and tool costs) and their description, in your game language.

### Moving Items

- **Take and store with one click.** RMB takes a stack from the chests or stores a stack from your backpack.
- **Drag and drop** with LMB between the two sides. Hold **Shift** when you let go to move every stack of that item.
- **Drop onto your hotbars**: items go to hotbar 1, then hotbar 2, then your backpack. If all three are full, nothing moves.
- Drag between your hotbars and your inventory, too.
- Stored items go to the chest that already holds the most of them, otherwise the nearest one with room. Gear keeps its level and upgrades: every move is the game's own.

### Use from Chests

- **MMB** (or the Use button) uses a food, drink, potion, bandage or scroll exactly as from your hotbar: the animation plays and the buff shows in the buff panel with its real effects and duration.
- Works on items in chests (moved into your backpack first), in your backpack and on your hotbars.

### Favorites

- **Shift + RMB** marks an item as a favorite, in the mod's window **and** in the game's own inventory, chest and station screens. With a controller, press **L3** on the selected slot.
- Favorites get a **gold slot background** in your inventory and chest screens, drawn by the game itself so it stays behind the game's menus. They are listed first, and **stay in your backpack** when you use the game's Deposit All, Deposit Stacks or a Quick Stack Station.
- **Gear favorites are per rarity**, so favoriting your Legendary staff doesn't protect the Uncommon copy you just picked up.
- The **Construction Hammer**, the **Summoning Staff**, and the **Overgrowth** and **Decay** tools can be favorited too, whatever they currently have selected.

### Chest names that mean something

- Name a chest after a category (*Weapons*, *Meals*, *Ores*) or a whole group (*Gear*, *Materials*) and Quick Deposit and Re-Sort send it exactly that.
- **Rename from the window**: the name column is a dropdown of every category name. RMB on it to type a custom name instead. Names are the game's own, so they are saved with the world and everyone sees them.
- **Specific before general**: a chest named *Weapons* fills before one named *Gear*. When every chest of the best name is full, the next one takes over.
- **Catch-all chest**: name a chest *All* and it takes any item that no other chest's name asks for, or whose chests are full. *All* is first in the dropdown. Auto-Name Chests never uses it.
- Start a chest's name with **--** and the mod never puts anything in it.
- **Auto-Name Chests** (optional): when nothing has room for an item, the closest chest that still has its default name is named for it, either by sub-category (*Weapons*) or by group (*Gear*).

### Quick Deposit

- Inside a base, press **Sort Inventory twice** (G by default, or LT + X) or use a **Quick Stack Station**, and your backpack empties into the base's chests.
- The **Quick Deposit button** in the window sends your backpack to your linked chests, wherever you are.
- **Auto Quick Deposit** (optional): when loot fills your backpack, a quick deposit runs by itself (at most every 10 seconds). Only looting triggers it, not taking from your own chests or crafting.
- Existing stacks are topped up first, then items go to a chest named for their category, then to a chest that already holds them.
- Never touched: your hotbars, what you wear, your favorites, chests named with **--**, and Magic Chests with Receive Quick Stacking turned off.
- **Quick Deposit and Auto Salvage**: set rules for Weapons, Shields, Armor and Rings, matching items get deposited, the rest remain in your inventory. Set up auto salvage and "the rest" can be salvaged when you loot it. (Note that it reaches your inventory first, so you still unlock recipes for items that you loot.)
- A **report** tells you what went where and what stayed, including which chest name is missing ("No chest named Ores (Iron Ore, Copper Ore)").
- The chests that received items are **highlighted** with the game's own outline, **visible through walls**.

### Re-Sort Chests

- One button moves every item sitting in the wrong linked chest into a linked chest whose name asks for it. Items no chest asks for stay where they are.

### Categories overview

- Every category with a show/hide checkbox, how many of its items your linked chests hold, whether a chest is named for it (and how many), and how many free slots those chests have left.
- **LMB on a category** highlights every chest named for it in the world. LMB on a group highlights the group's chests and all of its sub-categories' chests.
- Materials and Building blocks are hidden by default, since you mostly use them through the crafting menu and the Construction Hammer. A search still finds them.

### Auto-Stations

- Name a Magic Chest **Auto-Stations** in a base, and the mod keeps it stocked from your linked chests in other bases with what that base's automated stations (Forge, Smelter, Bonemeal...) need for their selected recipes. The game's own station buttons, and mods like Busy Hands, then fill the stations from it.
- **Auto-Stations Crafts** sets how many crafts' worth to keep (10 by default, 0 turns it off) and **Auto-Stations Every** how often it tops up (30 seconds by default). Once the stations have used half of an item, it restocks right away.
- It counts every Magic Chest of the base, so nothing moves while the base already has enough. Favorites never move.
- With **Auto-Name Chests** on, the base's unnamed Magic Chest closest to its stations is named Auto-Stations for you. Otherwise a message tells you to name one.
- Quick Deposit and Re-Sort leave Auto-Stations chests alone.

### Cross-Base Storage &amp; Craft

- You can craft (at stations, NPCs and from your inventory) from any base, from your linked chests, and use their dyes at the coloring station. Since Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.12 this works in every crafting menu without [Cross-Base Storage](https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/245), even next to Building Tools.
- **Fill Stations From Linked Chests**: a production station's +1 and +10 also take from your linked chests what your backpack and the base's own chests can't cover.
- **Build From Linked Chests**: the Construction Hammer and the build menu count and use the blocks and materials your linked chests hold.
- **Lockpicks From Linked Chests**: a lock that needs a lockpick opens with one held in your linked chests.
- Your backpack and the base's own chests are always used first. Each option can be turned off in the Settings tab.

### Settings in the window

- A Settings tab with every option and an explanation on hover. Changes apply at once and are saved. The same settings are also on the mod's page in Kiln's menu.

---

## How to Use

### Getting started

1. Load a world you host (single player counts) and press **F2**.
2. Open the **Chests** tab. Tick the chests you want, or press **Link Nearby Chests** to link everything within the Link Radius (100 m by default). You can also press **Link Chest** in a chest's own screen. Linking moves nothing; it only adds the chest to the list.
3. Go back to the **Items** tab. Everything in your linked chests is now on the left, your hotbars and backpack on the right.

Only Magic Chests are offered for linking by default. Turn on **Link Regular Chests** in the Settings tab to link regular chests too.

### Controls in the window

- **LMB** : select an item (its buttons appear above the list: Take Stack, Take All, Store, Use, Favorite)
- **RMB** : take a stack from the chests, or store a stack from your backpack
- **Shift + RMB** : mark or unmark a favorite
- **MMB**: use the item (food, drinks, potions, bandages, scrolls)
- **Drag &amp; Drop** : move a stack to the other side. Hold **Shift** when you release to move every stack. Drop on the Hotbars list to fill hotbar 1, then 2, then the backpack.
- **Hover** : item details and which chests hold it
- **Drag the bar** between the two sides : resize them
- **Escape** or **F2** : close the window

### Controls in the game's own screens

- **Shift + RMB** on a slot (or **L3** on the selected slot with a controller) marks or unmarks its item as a favorite.
- **Sort Inventory twice** (G G) inside a base: Quick Deposit.

### Setting up sorted storage

1. In the **Chests** tab, pick a category name from each chest's name dropdown (*Weapons*, *Meals*, *Ores*...). Use the **Show** button to see which chest is which in the world.
2. Open the **Categories** tab to check which categories have a chest and how much room is left. LMB a category to light up its chests.
3. Press **Re-Sort Chests** once to move what you already own into the right chests.
4. From then on, **G G** in your base, or the Quick Deposit button anywhere, keeps it sorted. Turn on **Auto Quick Deposit** and it happens on its own whenever loot fills your backpack.

Tip : turn on **Auto-Name Chests** in the Settings tab and drop a few unnamed chests in your base. The mod names them as it needs them.

### Changing the key

The key is **Open Streamlined Logistics** in the Keys tab of Kiln's menu.

---

## Requirements

- [Kiln](https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln) mod loader, **0.2.0-dev.31.12 or newer**.

## Installation

1. Close the game.
2. Add the archive through Kiln.
3. Start the game. The mod shows up in Kiln's Mods page. It has its own settings menu inside its F2 menu, so you don't have to go through Kiln for that.

To update, check with Kiln or download the newest version and install it manually.

## Compatibility

- **Works in a world you host** (single player or as the host). Joining someone else's world and dedicated servers are not supported yet.
- **XHL-Remote Chest**: Streamlined Logistics replaces it and does not need XHL-Core. They don't share links. Running both is not recommended.
- **Quick Deposit (Greeneye)**: while it is installed and enabled, this mod's own G G deposit stands down and leaves it to Quick Deposit.
- **Custom categories**: if a **chestsort\_categories.json** sits next to the game's exe (the file Quick Deposit uses), the material categories are read from it and follow your edits live. Otherwise the copy bundled with the mod is used.

## Known limitations

- Links are stored by chest position and are not yet kept per world.
- The repair kit can't be used from the window; use it from your hotbar.
- The game's full item detail (damage, perks, gems) only shows for items you have looked at in the game's own screens this session.
- No controller button to open the window yet, nor controller navigation.
- A large Re-Sort takes a little while; the window's other buttons wait until it ends.

## Planned features

These are designed and waiting on a Kiln update that gives mods what they need. They will come as soon as Kiln supports them.

- **Use the repair kit** from the window, like other consumables.

